## How to reproduce

1. Verify the package (stops on any mismatch):

   ```
   python scripts/reproduce.py --package . --verify-only
   ```

2. Rebuild the environment. See `env/REBUILD.md`. To print the commands:

   ```
   python scripts/reproduce.py --package . --rebuild --dry-run
   ```

3. Get the weights: `${repo_id}` at revision `${revision}`. Weights are not included.
   They are referenced by ID and SHA-256 in `manifest.yaml` (`model.weight_files`).

4. Re-run the archived scripts and compare with the archived labels:

   ```
   ${reproduce_command}
   ```

   Add `--sample 20` for a quick check on a deterministic sample.
   The report is written to `reproduction/REPRODUCTION_REPORT.md`.

5. Prompt stability (repeats, and researcher-written paraphrases of `prompts/prompt.yaml`):

   ```
   python scripts/stability.py --package . --engine <engine> --sample 50 --repeats 3 --paraphrase v1.yaml
   ```

